{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver cancelled TRP-06052 for rider no-show without ever sending an in-app chat message. The chat log for this trip holds exactly one message and it was sent by the rider (MSG-06052-001, 'Coming down in 3 min', 14:23:40) — the driver sent none, and the trip record's derived contact_before_cancel.message_count for the driver is 0. POL-NS-23 makes a driver-sent in-app message a condition of charging the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06052", "EV-TRIP-06052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23's contact obligation is conjunctive: the driver must have sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call, both before cancelled_at. The two unanswered in-app calls at 14:24:30 and 14:26:50 satisfy only the call limb; because the message limb is unmet the obligation as a whole is unmet — the trip record's own derived contact_before_cancel.obligation_met is false. On the clause's own terms the 5.00 SGD fee must be voided.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06052", "EV-CHAT-06052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Satisfying the free wait does not rescue the fee. On the record the driver marked arrival at 14:22:00 and cancelled at 14:28:05, 365 s later, so the 300 s free wait under POL-NS-21 was running from arrival and had expired (free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait = true). But POL-NS-22 permits the fee only 'when the driver cancels after the free wait', and POL-NS-23 layers a further, independent precondition on top: contact by message and call. A satisfied wait is necessary, not sufficient, and the fee stands or falls on POL-NS-23.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06052", "EV-GPS-06052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the contact obligation failed, POL-NS-23 fixes the consequence: the fee is voided and the rider is not charged — FULL_REFUND of the fee charged, with no driver compensation. The payments ledger shows a single cancellation-fee line of 5.00 SGD, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the entire contested 5.00 SGD is still outstanding and is what the rider is owed under POL-GEN-03.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-06052", "EV-TRIP-06052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The gap is not explained by the rider being uncontactable or absent from the app. The rider's message was read at 14:23:51, before either call was placed, so the driver had the rider's own in-app notice that she was on her way down and had an open chat channel in front of him; he simply never used it. The driver's counterparty statement ('Called 2 times, no pick up') is accurate as to the calls and silent on the message POL-NS-23 requires, so it does not answer the clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06052", "EV-TRIP-06052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[0].read_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "The 5.00 SGD no-show fee is voided and the rider is refunded in full. POL-NS-23 requires that, before cancelling for a no-show, the driver have both sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call to the rider, each before the cancellation. The call limb is met: the trip record carries two driver-placed in-app calls, at 14:24:30 (rang 22 s) and 14:26:50 (rang 18 s), both before cancelled_at 14:28:05 (EV-TRIP-06052). The message limb fails: the complete chat log (EV-CHAT-06052, weight 1.0) holds exactly one message and it was sent by the rider — 'Coming down in 3 min' at 14:23:40 — and the trip record's contact_before_cancel block reports message_count 0 with obligation_met false. Because POL-NS-23's obligation is conjunctive, and one limb is missing, the clause voids the fee and the rider is not charged: the whole contested 5.00 SGD is returned. The payments ledger (EV-FARE-06052) shows a single cancellation-fee line of 5.00, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the entire 5.00 SGD is outstanding and is what the rider is owed. No driver compensation attaches, as POL-NS-23 expressly provides for FULL_REFUND with none. The rider's claims on the unmet message limb, the conjunctive reading of the obligation, and the resulting full refund are accepted. The rider's further point that her message was read at 14:23:51 (before either call) is accepted and confirms the driver had an open in-app channel he did not use. The driver's claims are answered: the GPS trace (EV-GPS-06052) does corroborate the 14:22:00 arrival (nearest fix 3.28 m from the pickup, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius) and the free wait did run 300 s from arrival and expire at 14:27:05 with cancellation at 14:28:05 (365 s) — these facts are accepted — but a satisfied wait is necessary, not sufficient: POL-NS-23 layers the message-plus-call precondition on top, and the driver's own submission concedes the message limb. The driver's POL-NS-24 argument is accepted: that clause governs a rider's cancellation following a driver no-show and gives no route here, and its goodwill limb is in any event excluded by the two attempted calls. The fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD policy amount (fee_matches_policy true, policy_fee_sgd 5.00), so POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not fire. The POL-NS-25 repeat no-show flag does not fire because the fee does not stand, and POL-NS-24's goodwill limb does not apply. No referral is produced by any clause on these facts.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

