    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both accounts of the sequence agree, and the record confirms it. The driver marked arrival at 14:22:00; on this on-demand trip the 300-second free wait under POL-NS-21 ran from that arrival, the driver placed two in-app calls (14:24:30, ringing 22 s, and 14:26:50, ringing 18 s, both unanswered), and he cancelled for rider no-show at 14:28:05 — 365 s after the wait began and after it had expired at 14:27:05. The 5.00 SGD no-show fee was charged (EV-FARE-06052: one cancellation-fee line of 5.00, total_charged 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00).\n\nThat does not settle the fee, because POL-NS-23 puts an independent precondition on it: before cancelling for no-show the driver must have sent at least one in-app chat message to the rider AND placed at least one in-app call, both before cancelled_at, and if either is missing the fee is voided. The complete chat log (EV-CHAT-06052, weight 1.0, no issue codes) holds exactly one message and it was sent by the rider — MSG-06052-001, 'Coming down in 3 min', at 14:23:40, read at 14:23:51. The driver sent none; the trip record (EV-TRIP-06052, weight 1.0) reports contact_before_cancel.message_count 0 and obligation_met false. The call limb is satisfied but the message limb is not, and the obligation is conjunctive. On the clause's own terms the fee is voided and the rider is not charged.\n\nI therefore rule FULL_REFUND of the 5.00 SGD the rider was charged, with no driver compensation. The driver's points are accepted as facts — the arrival mark is corroborated by the GPS trace within the 50 m STANDARD radius, the free wait was honoured in full, two in-app calls were attempted, and the rider was given until 14:28:05 to board — but none of them answers POL-NS-23, which layers a further requirement on top of a satisfied wait. POL-NS-22's DRIVER_COMPENSATION outcome applies only where the fee stands, and it does not here. POL-NS-24 is not the rider's route: this trip was cancelled by the driver, not by the rider after a driver no-show, and its goodwill limb would in any event be excluded because contact was attempted; the refund rests on POL-NS-23 alone.\n\nNo referral arises. The charge is exactly the 5.00 SGD policy fee, so POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not fire; the POL-NS-24 goodwill credit does not apply because the driver did attempt contact; and the POL-NS-25 repeat no-show flag is not engaged — the counter field is not present on the rider profile, and in any case this fee does not stand. The contested value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's first band, so under POL-NS-26 this AI ruling is final.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
